From 017ba77a09dcca493adabdfe94fb3dd201089d41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:02:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] imem-access: report seekable callbacks as fast-seekable

libvlc_media_new_callbacks media were never fast-seekable, so the input
put the prefetch filter in front of them. With its defaults it reads
16 MiB per request in a thread of its own before the first picture, and
serves a seek from that buffer. An application whose callbacks answer
seeks serves its bytes like a file, and is read like one: straight
through, as a local file is.
---
 modules/access/imem-access.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/access/imem-access.c b/modules/access/imem-access.c
index 25547c1..418827a 100644
--- a/modules/access/imem-access.c
+++ b/modules/access/imem-access.c
@@ -79,7 +79,10 @@ static int Control(stream_t *access, int query, va_list args)
             break;
 
         case STREAM_CAN_FASTSEEK:
-            *va_arg(args, bool *) = false;
+            /* An application that answers seeks serves its bytes like a file:
+             * reads go straight through, as for a local file, rather than
+             * through the prefetch filter's large background reads. */
+            *va_arg(args, bool *) = sys->seek_cb != NULL;
             break;
 
         case STREAM_CAN_PAUSE:
-- 
